Enumerate the fTPM without waiting for tee-supplicant

The TA is marked TA_FLAG_DEVICE_ENUM_SUPP, so the kernel only learns
about it once tee-supplicant is running. On the i.MX8MP EVK that lands
around 13 s into boot, long after IMA has looked for a TPM (2.9 s) and
concluded there is none - a decision it never revisits, which leaves the
measurement log unanchored for the rest of the boot.

The flag exists because the TA's storage used to require the supplicant.
That is no longer true when OP-TEE reaches RPMB from the core, so switch
to TA_FLAG_DEVICE_ENUM, which enumerates the device while the OP-TEE
driver probes.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [depends on a platform-specific storage
backend that is not upstream]

--- a/Samples/ARM32-FirmwareTPM/optee_ta/fTPM/user_ta_header_defines.h
+++ b/Samples/ARM32-FirmwareTPM/optee_ta/fTPM/user_ta_header_defines.h
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@

 #define TA_UUID                     TA_FTPM_UUID

-#define TA_FLAGS                    (TA_FLAG_SINGLE_INSTANCE | TA_FLAG_INSTANCE_KEEP_ALIVE | TA_FLAG_DEVICE_ENUM_SUPP)
+#define TA_FLAGS                    (TA_FLAG_SINGLE_INSTANCE | TA_FLAG_INSTANCE_KEEP_ALIVE | TA_FLAG_DEVICE_ENUM)
 #define TA_STACK_SIZE               (64 * 1024)
 #define TA_DATA_SIZE                (32 * 1024)

